[Music]  while tom hardy's dual performances  eddie brock and venom might have stolen  your attention venom let there be  carnage has some pretty important  characters and relatively minor roles  some pay tribute to the comics while  others might hint at future film stories  here are the characters that mean more  than you realize in venom keep in mind  heavy spoilers follow  portrayed by striking white-haired  veteran uk tv actor shan weber dr pazzo  is the cruel uncaring administrator  behind the endless incarceration of  inmates like francis barrison at the  beginning of let there be carnage she's  there to accept shriek when she arrives  decades later she's still at ravencroft  when cletus cassidy comes to rescue the  love of his life carnage's tentacles  lift dr pazzo off the ground and  strangle the not-so-good doctor while  the baddies make a prison break the  character has a small but noteworthy  history in marvel comics beginning with  1995's venom carnage unleashed volume 1  number 1. in that comic she's introduced  as a psychiatrist for cletus cassidy  rather than shriek by 1996 paso was  being presented as something of an  expert on symbiotes advising the police  and trying to help solve murders that  was pretty much the last appearance of  the character until now and let there be  carnage there are multiple references to  cassidy's abuse at his father's hands  how he murdered his grandmother and even  the family dog while the details have  been changed a bit without the pazzo  character in the comic books we wouldn't  have a lot of that information so in  essence the movie has shifted paso's  focus from cassidy to barrison and  turned her into much more of an evil  prison warden-like character  portrayed by veteran character actor  stephen graham patrick mulligan plays a  pivotal role in all the lives of the  film's main characters he can first be  seen in flashback that opens the film as  francis barristan is being moved from  saint estes reform school to ravencroft  while attempting to make an escape from  a moving vehicle mulligan shoots shriek  in the eye thinking he's killed her and  nearly losing his hearing in the battle  decades later the now detective mulligan  is overseeing the escalating crime  investigations around san francisco he's  suspicious of eddie brock but unaware  that he has a murderous symbiote sharing  his body instead mulligan just seems to  think eddie is a weird dude why would he  think that i have proof  [Music]  well fair enough when eddie realizes  that cletus cassidy is on a mission to  free francis barrison mulligan insists  that she's dead but soon learns the  truth and also discovers that shriek has  been holding a serious grudge against  him this all culminates in an engraved  invitation to the so-called red wedding  where mulligan is a guest of honor after  the inevitable showdown with shriek  mulligan lives to fight another day but  seems to have developed glowing blue  eyes and a fascination with the word  monster unless you think mulligan is  just another generic cop he is likely  based on patrick mulligan a prominent  character in venom and carnage comics  from the 2000s his story began in venom  carnage number one and number two as  carnage birthed the symbiote that would  come to be known as toxin mulligan a new  york city cop became its host and  expectations were that toxin would  become a hero because of mulligan's  career but as time went on mulligan  developed a fear and paranoia about  having toxin around his wife and newborn  son and although he assisted heroes like  spider-man and the avengers he struggled  with his newfound powers even allowing  toxin at one point to murder a criminal  eventually mulligan himself was killed  and the symbiote toxin went on to other  hosts de mulligan's glowing blue eyes  indicate that steven graham might have  some toxic behavior ahead of him while  marvel fans might hope so we'll likely  have to wait until the next venom movie  to learn more  during what has to be the most surreal  scene of venom let there be carnage the  recently separated venom infiltrates  what looks to be some kind of pride  adjacent rave where its inhabitants  assume the symbiote is a person in a  really cool costume it then drunkenly  storms the stage rants about eddie and  becomes a hero to those in attendance  posters publicizing the event lists the  talent as little sims and that is who  venom takes the microphone away from mid  performance the 27 year old british  nigerian artist is no character but in  fact an experimental rapper who has  opened for the likes of gorillas earned  praise from kendrick lamar and appeared  previously on the netflix show top boy  in the bbc children's series spirit  warriors little sims also released a  song in 2019 called venom which doesn't  seem to directly reference alien  symbiotes but is peppered with so many  words that can't be repeated in this  video that all you need to know is the  chorus is a multiple repetition of the  word venom shortly before venom let  there be carnage arrived in theaters she  released her fourth studio album  entitled sometimes i might be introvert  according to director andy circus the  little sims cameo came about because of  tom hardy circus told uprox she actually  had made a song unbeknownst to her  called venom that connected very much  with the first movie and so tom got in  touch with her and that song became sort  of the focus circus revealed that the  scene was originally written not as a  rave but a quote carnival of the damned  party who is credited on the film not  only as a star but also a co-writer  sounds like he was a driving force  behind the scene tom and co-writer kelly  marcel were always about venom coming  out and going to a party that was very  sort of an lgbtqia kind of festival this  is venom's coming out party check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about venom are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  you

